### 5. Non‑Functional Business Requirements

| Requirement | Business Rationale |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Fully dynamic input** | No pre‑loaded teams or players – the commissioner builds the league from scratch each season. This makes the tool reusable for different sports (switch from soccer to basketball by changing position names only). |
| **Real‑time standings update** | After every finalized match, the league table must be recalculated instantly – the coordinator can print it to the console to show teams during the post‑match huddle. |
| **Audit via enumeration** | When displaying the match schedule for the weekend, each match is numbered (via `enumerate`) so the coordinator can say “I need to reschedule match #4” and the system references it easily. |
| **Scout‑friendly output** | Searching for a player must display their full stats: total goals, assists, cards, and which team they play for – all aggregated from the nested match events list. |
| **Session‑only data** | Designed for a single season. At the end of the season, the coordinator can manually copy the final standings and award winners before closing the program. |

