### 6. How This Sports Business Naturally Uses Your Required Python Features

| Required Feature | Where It Emerges in PlayMaker’s Business Logic |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Data types** | `dict` for teams, players, venues, and matches; `list` of tuples for in‑match events (goal, minute); `set` for jersey numbers (to enforce uniqueness per team) and player IDs (to prevent dual registration). |
| **All operators** | Arithmetic (`+`, `-`, `/`) for goal difference, points per game, and average goals; comparison (`>=`, `<=`) for squad size limits and venue capacity checks; logical (`and`, `or`) for combining venue availability + team availability in one scheduling decision; membership (`in`) to check if a player is already rostered; identity (`is not None`) when retrieving a match record. |
| **Control flows** | Main `while` menu loop for the commissioner; `if-elif-else` for menu options; `for` loops to iterate through match events to calculate player stats. |
| **Nested data structures** | `match` → `{'home_team': id, 'away_team': id, 'events': [(pid, 'goal', 23), ...]}`. `team` → `{'players': [pid1, pid2, ...]}`. This nesting is essential. |
| **Nested loops & conditions** | When calculating a player’s total goals, you loop over all matches, then inside that loop loop over all `events` (nested loop), and check if `event[1] == 'Goal'` (nested condition) – this is exactly how sports stat engines work. |
| **`enumerate()`** | Used when showing the upcoming match schedule with numbering, and when listing all players in a team so the commissioner can select a player to update their stats. |
| **`Counter()`** | Used for the **Golden Boot** (goal scoring), **Playmaker** (assists), **Fair Play** (cards per team), and **Venue utilization** – four distinct, business‑critical counters. |
| **Error handling** | Every numeric input (minutes, jersey numbers, ages) uses `try-except`. Dictionary lookups for team/player existence use `.get()` with `None` checks to prevent `KeyError`. This ensures the league commissioner never loses data to a crash. |
| **Search feature** | Search is vital here – the commissioner constantly searches for a player by name to check if they are suspended, or searches for a venue to see its upcoming schedule before booking a final. |

